  "description": "What makes the difference between a great bean salad and a boring bowlful of beans? The answer is simple: Go for maximum contrast, both in texture and in flavor. Here, I add layers of crispness and crunch with almonds, radish, radicchio, fresh parsley, scallion, and quick-pickled onion.",
  "notes": "Notes: If using dried beans, 0.34 kg dried will yield approximately 4 cups cooked. If using canned, 3 (425 g) cans should provide the 4 cups cooked beans called for here. Read more on dried-to-cooked/canned bean conversions here. To cook dried beans, soak overnight (or, if you're short on time, bring to a boil in a pot of water), then drain. Add plenty of fresh cold water to cover, along with aromatics like onion, garlic, and carrots, and season with salt; bring to a simmer and cook until beans are tender.",
